# Register a new object in the world (perception saw something new).
# held_by is deliberately absent: "which gripper holds this object" is robot
# proprioception owned by the backend (set_held_by), not something perception
# observes. A newly added object is registered as held by nobody.
# Refused (success=false) for an object_id already in the scene, a non-identifier
# label/object_id, or a pose the store rejects.
string object_id
string label
geometry_msgs/Pose pose
bool graspable
---
# success=true means the write committed to disk, error is empty.
# success=false means the store refused and the scene is byte-identical;
# error names the reason.
bool success
string error
